{% set local_problem %}
<p>Monrovia's humid climate is tough on exposed wood. When gutters leak or overflow, water runs behind them and soaks fascia boards. Over time, that repeated moisture causes rot that can spread to rafters if not addressed.</p>

<p>Both older and newer Monrovia homes can have fascia problems. Established homes may have decades of accumulated damage. Newer homes often have damage from builder-grade gutters that leaked within a few years of construction.</p>

<p>Installing new gutters on damaged fascia is a waste of money. The gutters won't stay properly attached, and underlying rot continues spreading. We fix the foundation first.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>We start with thorough inspection, checking fascia and soffit for water damage, soft spots, and rot. We'll show you what we find.</p>

<p>For damaged areas, we remove existing gutters, cut out bad wood, and install new fascia using quality materials. Then we install new gutters on the solid foundation.</p>

<p>The result is complete protection from fascia to downspout, with one warranty covering everything.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've been repairing fascia and installing gutters in Monrovia for over 20 years. We handle both jobs, which means better coordination, cleaner work, and single-point accountability.</p>

<p>We're just 12 miles away and can schedule quickly.</p>
{% endset %}

